        "SignificantEvents": "Observed fire behavior today was moderate on the eastern side of the fire (Div R and T). Backing, flanking, with isolated torching, was observed in interior pockets of timber stands. Creeping and smoldering from the burnout two days ago was also observed. No movement in grass fuels occurred.",
        "SummaryFuelModel": "Timber fuels are extremely dry and conducive to fire spread. Shrub and grass fuels are also burning quite readily. ERC?s across the forest are just below the 90th percentile. 1000-hr fuels are at 8%.",
