        "UniqueFireIdentifier": "2026-UTMLF-005112",
        "WeatherConcerns": "Moisture remains overhead on Saturday with additional isolated to scattered showers and thunderstorms anticipated. Chances peak during the mid to late afternoon into the evening hours. Primary concerns with this activity include lightning, erratic outflow winds, and heavy downpours. Heavy rainfall over the burn scar, especially where burn severity is great, may lead to localized flash flooding and/or debris flows. High temperatures rise into the low to mid 70s (Highest elevations) to mid 80s (lower slopes) with minimum RHs in the 32-40% range. General winds begin out of the SSW becoming variable and potentially gusty in the afternoon and evening due to outflow winds traversing the region. Daily thunderstorm chances persist through the middle of next week. ",
