        "SignificantEvents": "Observed fire behavior today was minimal around the perimeter.  Backing, flanking, with isolated interior torching remains possible within interior pockets of timber stands; otherwise creeping and smoldering is expected.  No movement in grass fuels occurred. ",
        "SummaryFuelModel": "Timber fuels remain dry and are still conducive to fire spread.  Shrub and grass fuels have recovered with the higher humidities and won?t readily burn until drier air settles in.  ERCs across the forest are around the 80th percentile. 1000-hr fuels are at 9%. ",
        "TotalIncidentPersonnel": 845,
        "UniqueFireIdentifier": "2026-UTMLF-005112",
        "WeatherConcerns": "Thunderstorms dropped a wetting less than 0.10 rainfall across most of the fire yesterday with additional chances for precipitation the rest of the weekend. Additional shower and thunderstorm activity is anticipated during the afternoon hours on today and Sunday, peaking between 1600 and 2000. Primary concerns with this activity includes lightning, erratic outflow winds, and heavy downpours. Heavy rainfall over the burnscar, especially where burn severity is great, may lead to localized flash flooding and/or debris flows. High temperatures rise into the mid 70s to low 80s Sunday with minimum RHs in the 35-42% range. General winds begin out of the SSW becoming variable and potentially gusty in the afternoon and evening due to outflow winds traversing the region. Temperatures warm slightly on Mon/Tues while T-storm chances persist.�",
