        "TotalIncidentPersonnel": 1467,
        "UniqueFireIdentifier": "2026-UTMLF-005112",
        "WeatherConcerns": "Expect a significant pattern change Sunday as general winds shift direction and thunderstorm chances return (east to west storm motion). Isolated to scattered thunderstorms in the afternoon may produce lightning and strong/erratic outflow winds. Active plume growth and mid-level moisture will support conditional pyrocumulonimbus development. High temperatures rise in the mid to upper 80s with minimum RHs in the 13-20% range. General winds begin rather breezy/gusty out of the SE, especially along ridgetops and aligned drainages, before decreasing into the afternoon. However, there is moderate confidence these gusty SE winds return the second half of the overnight period into Monday AM.",
