        "SignificantEvents": "Observed fire behavior today was minimal around the perimeter. Smoldering and creeping with very isolated interior torching possible. Otherwise, continued smoldering and creeping is expected. No movement in grass fuels occurred.",
        "SummaryFuelModel": "Timber fuels have begun reacting to the precipitation over the fire and are now less conducive to fire spread. Shrub and grass fuels have recovered with the higher humidities and won?t readily burn until less precipitation occurs and drier air settles in. ERCs across the forest are around the 50th percentile. 1000-hr fuels are at 14%.",
        "TotalIncidentPersonnel": 126,
        "UniqueFireIdentifier": "2026-UTMLF-005112",
        "WeatherConcerns": "The risk for heavy rainfall and flash flooding continues through this evening. Dry air begins to move into the region on Thursday. This will dampen the risk of flash flooding, but afternoon convection remains likely as it will take a couple of days to scour remnant moisture out of the atmosphere. In general, look for warming temperatures, decreasing RH, and decreasing chances for showers and storms late this week into the weekend. \n\n",
